{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CevFaYmMYxGgpQWesE9cQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on my analysis, I now understand the repository structure and conventions. Let me move to the design phase.\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n```\n\n**Proposed change, file by file:**\n\n1. **ApiError.kt** - Add a new error code `SHIPMENT_CANNOT_CONFIRM` to the ErrorCode enum. This will be used when attempting to confirm a shipment that is in CANCELLED status.\n\n2. **ShipmentController.kt** - Add a new `@PostMapping(\"/{shipmentId}/confirm\")` endpoint that:\n   - Takes `shipmentId` as a path variable\n   - Looks up the shipment (throws ResourceNotFoundException if not found)\n   - If status is CANCELLED, throws ConflictException with SHIPMENT_CANNOT_CONFIRM\n   - If status is CREATED, updates to CONFIRMED and saves\n   - If status is CONFIRMED, returns as-is (idempotent)\n   - Returns ResponseEntity.ok(shipment) with the result\n\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** - Add four new test cases:\n   - `confirms a created shipment and transitions to CONFIRMED status`\n   - `confirms an already confirmed shipment without changing anything (idempotency)`\n   - `rejects confirming a cancelled shipment with HTTP 409`\n   - `rejects confirming a non-existent shipment with HTTP 404`\n\n**Alternative rejected:** I considered whether to add a service layer to encapsulate the confirmation logic, but this would be unrelated refactoring - the existing endpoints directly use the repository in the controller, so the confirm endpoint should follow that same pattern.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n1. **Happy path (CREATED → CONFIRMED):**\n   - Request: POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm\n   - Repository lookup: findById(shipmentId) → Shipment(status=CREATED)\n   - Update: save(shipment.copy(status=CONFIRMED))\n   - Response: 200 OK with updated shipment\n\n2. **Idempotent case (CONFIRMED):**\n   - Request: POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm\n   - Repository lookup: findById(shipmentId) → Shipment(status=CONFIRMED)\n   - Action: return as-is, no save needed\n   - Response: 200 OK with unchanged shipment\n\n3. **Conflict case (CANCELLED):**\n   - Request: POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm\n   - Repository lookup: findById(shipmentId) → Shipment(status=CANCELLED)\n   - Exception: throw ConflictException(SHIPMENT_CANNOT_CONFIRM)\n   - Response: 409 Conflict with error envelope\n\n4. **Not found case:**\n   - Request: POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm\n   - Repository lookup: findById(shipmentId) → null\n   - Exception: throw ResourceNotFoundException(SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND)\n   - Response: 404 Not Found with error envelope\n\n**Test strategy:**\n- Test 1: Create shipment, confirm it, verify status changed to CONFIRMED\n- Test 2: Create shipment, confirm twice, verify second confirm returns 200 with CONFIRMED status\n- Test 3: Insert cancelled shipment directly into repository, attempt to confirm, verify 409 with SHIPMENT_CANNOT_CONFIRM code\n- Test 4: Attempt to confirm non-existent shipment, verify 404 with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND code\n\n```\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n```\n\nNow I'll implement the changes:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":873,"cache_read_input_tokens":19184,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":873},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"661db1fc-2684-4847-b4e7-e094f3d827c3","uuid":"40d6c4f7-f07f-41c9-b0df-3c68106a702a","timestamp":"2026-09-10T18:43:48.432Z","request_id":"req_011CevFaYA94xa3TLYtCUSuB"}
